>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must have at most 2 dimensions to avoid t() 3D error)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≤ 2
>>
Rule 2 (explicitly enumerate valid dimensionalities)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 1 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 2
>>
Rule 3 (non-negative sizes for 2D tensors; 0D/1D allowed as is)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (all existing shape dimensions are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (input tensor has a recognized dtype code)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 12
>>
Rule 7 (explicitly reject tensors with 3 or more dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 then false
>>
Rule 9 (input tensor has a supported numerical dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
